0007:     """
0008:     Draw the red row and column dividers through two marker pixels and fill the marked rectangle interior blue.
0009: 
0010:     Input structure:
0011:     - The grid has a uniform background and exactly two non-background marker pixels.
0012:     - The two markers occupy different rows and different columns, making opposite corners of a nonempty rectangle.
0013:     - The marker color is preserved as the divider color, while blue is absent from the input and used for the fill.
0014: 
0015:     Rule:
0016:     - Use the two marker rows and two marker columns as full-width/full-height dividers.
0017:     - Paint those rows and columns with the marker color.
0018:     - Paint the strict interior of the rectangle between the marker rows and columns blue.
0019: 
0020:     Key insight:
0021:     - The isolated markers are opposite rectangle corners; extending their horizontal and vertical projections partitions the whole grid.
0022:     """
0023:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
